    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As mentioned before, methods mean functions when working with classes. Let's see how we can add a method to the Student class."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1class Student:\n2\n3\n4    # add a method to check pass/fail\n5    def check_pass_fail(self):\n6        if self.score >= 40:\n7            return True\n8        else:\n9            return False\n10\n11\n12# create objects\n13student1 = Student()\n14\n15# add attributes\n16student1.name = 'Harry'\n17student1.score = 85"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, we have created the check_pass_fail() method inside the Student class. Now, any object of the student class (such as student1 in the above code) can access this method."
    },
